  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1993-p16.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Starting inside, \\(2 + \\dfrac13 = \\dfrac73,\\) so \\(\\dfrac{1}{\\frac{7}{3}} = \\dfrac37.\\)\n\nThen \\(1 + \\dfrac37 = \\dfrac{10}{7},\\) and the whole expression is \\(\\dfrac{1}{\\frac{10}{7}} = \\dfrac{7}{10}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C .",
      "hints": [
        "Work from the bottom up: first simplify \\(2 + \\dfrac13\\)",
        "Then \\(1 + \\dfrac{1}{\\frac{7}{3}} = 1 + \\dfrac37,\\) and take the reciprocal"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
